WEBVTT

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:12.839
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning all. You alright? Quick one today, yeah? Before we start, whoever left a birthday cake in the office is now my favourite person.</v>

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:17.679
<v Callum Reid>Wasn't me, but I've had a slice already, for quality purposes.</v>

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:24.359
<v Jamie Brennan>Lucky you. I couldn't even get a brew, the broken coffee machine in the canteen's still dead.</v>

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.800
<v Grace Liu>That machine's got less uptime than some of our kit.</v>

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.370
<v Marcus Hale>Steady on, Grace.</v>

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, stand-up. Safety first, then production, then maintenance bits. Any incidents overnight?</v>

00:00:37.119 --> 00:00:46.920
<v Grace Liu>No incidents. I did notice the 11kV board was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down, so just an observation, not a job for today.</v>

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:56.020
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, and just on that, I tested the 11kV board yesterday and it's all fine now, so that's done already.</v>

00:00:57.729 --> 00:00:58.929
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Cheers. Production?</v>

00:01:01.409 --> 00:01:11.209
<v Callum Reid>Line one held okay after the wobble. Also, just so nobody plans around it, the shutdown on the line 3 barrel is cancelled now, production need it running.</v>

00:01:13.599 --> 00:01:16.049
<v Tomasz Nowak>Fine by me, I've got enough on.</v>

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:26.439
<v Callum Reid>And I noticed the compressor one was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Just keeping an eye, not asking for anything today.</v>

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:29.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, noted. Maintenance update, Tom?</v>

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:39.409
<v Tomasz Nowak>Finished the repair on the Injection Moulding Line 1 last night, so that's off the board. It was the feed issue in the end.</v>

00:01:41.349 --> 00:01:42.549
<v Sarah Okafor>Nice one, Tom.</v>

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:51.340
<v Marcus Hale>From CHP side, I've already swapped the filter on the GT1 Compressor Section yesterday, so don't duplicate that.</v>

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.040
<v Sarah Okafor>Good catch. Hannah, quality?</v>

00:01:54.200 --> 00:02:02.250
<v Hannah Price>Nothing dramatic. Only blocker is I can't get to the turbine one compressor until production gives us a window, so that's still stuck.</v>

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:06.450
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, not today, Hannah. We're flat out on that area.</v>

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:09.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, leave that parked then. Jamie, stores?</v>

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:18.919
<v Jamie Brennan>Bit of a pain, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the FLTs. I've chased again, but that's blocked waiting on them.</v>

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.539
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, thanks. Let's go through today's actions then.</v>

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:36.219
<v Sarah Okafor>First one, I'll replace the seals on the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit on the 3rd. It's not an emergency but don't let it slip, so I'll just keep that with me.</v>

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:40.270
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, fair. It's weeping but it's not pouring out yet.</v>

00:02:42.289 --> 00:02:44.740
<v Grace Liu>As long as it's tracked, that's fine.</v>

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:54.599
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll send the shift handover report round by the 28th. I didn't get that distribution cleaned up yesterday, so I'll do it.</v>

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:59.759
<v Jamie Brennan>Please copy me this time, I got the last one second hand.</v>

00:03:00.639 --> 00:03:01.840
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, will do.</v>

